<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.76 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.76 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Cotton Ginners Association said on Monday 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.761 million 375-lb bales by May 1, down from 9.938 million at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.674 (8.167)  2.087 (1.771)  8.761 (9.938)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.657 (8.166)  2.087 (1.769)  8.755 (9.935)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.897 (7.021)  1.950 (1.297)  7.838 (8.318)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.014 (0.949)  0.020 (1.390)  0.019 (1.494)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.772 (0.196)  0.130 (0.030)  0.902 (0.229)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
